@startuml

start

:Central ECU operates within safety-critical automotive context per ISO 26262;
:Manage subsystems via CAN and Ethernet networks;
fork
:Powertrain;
fork again
:BMS;
fork again
:Chassis;
end fork
:Utilize RTOS for priority-based scheduling of concurrent tasks;

if (Anomalous sensor data detected?) then (yes)
  :Initiate data verification process;

  fork
    :High-priority loop executes cyclic data integrity check;
    repeat
      :Continuously read from sensor ring buffer;
      :Validate data with CRC;
    repeat while (Data confirmed correct?) is (no)
  fork again
    :Lower-priority task performs data format verification against predefined schema;
  end fork

  if (Error confirmed?) then (yes)
    :Enter error handling state;
    fork
      :Mutex-protected logging task;
      :Classify and timestamp event in non-volatile memory;
    fork again
      :ISR-triggered alarm task;
      :Signal PMIC and FADEC according to fault level;
      :Potentially invoke limp-home mode;
    end fork
  else (no)
  end if

  :Perform final checksum processing;
  :Arm watchdog timer to guard against hangs;
  :Enter low-power standby state;
  :UDS/ISO-TP diagnostics remain available for interrogation;

else (no)
end if

:All actions time-stamped and persisted;
:Facilitate post-mortem analysis;

stop

@enduml
